  "description": "The meme weaponizes the trauma of the 2015 Paris terrorist attack to rhetorically justify Donald Trump's border wall proposal, implying that such a measure was 'obvious' or 'necessary' in light of the attack. This is harmful because it normalizes xenophobic or isolationist policies, risks trivializing the victims of the attack by reducing their suffering to a political talking point, and promotes a harmful political message by exploiting collective trauma.",
